1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,160
A student put four paper discs on a

2
00:00:02,240 --> 00:00:04,240
plate spread with bacteria.

3
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:07,120
Two days later, around disc A, a clear

4
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:09,840
zone twenty five millimetres across.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,160
Around disc B, fifteen.

6
00:00:12,320 --> 00:00:14,640
Around disc C, nothing.

7
00:00:14,760 --> 00:00:17,120
So is A the best medicine, and is

8
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:18,480
C useless?

9
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:20,160
The plate can't tell you either.

10
00:00:22,167 --> 00:00:24,246
Each disc holds a measured dose of an

11
00:00:24,327 --> 00:00:25,326
antibiotic.

12
00:00:25,607 --> 00:00:28,646
On the agar, the drug diffuses outwards, so

13
00:00:28,687 --> 00:00:31,526
it's strongest near the disc and weaker further

14
00:00:31,607 --> 00:00:31,926
out.

15
00:00:32,567 --> 00:00:34,486
Where it's strong enough to stop the bacteria

16
00:00:34,567 --> 00:00:36,806
growing, the agar stays clear.

17
00:00:37,367 --> 00:00:40,246
That clear ring is the zone of inhibition.

18
00:00:40,567 --> 00:00:42,646
At its edge, the drug has become too

19
00:00:42,727 --> 00:00:45,686
dilute, and beyond it the bacteria grow into

20
00:00:45,767 --> 00:00:46,886
a cloudy layer.

21
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:50,660
The aim is to compare the zones of

22
00:00:50,740 --> 00:00:54,420
inhibition that three antibiotic discs produce on one

23
00:00:54,580 --> 00:00:55,980
harmless bacterium.

24
00:00:56,260 --> 00:00:58,660
The independent variable is the antibiotic.

25
00:00:59,140 --> 00:01:01,940
The dependent variable is the zone's diameter, in

26
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:02,820
millimetres.

27
00:01:03,220 --> 00:01:06,020
Keep everything else the same: the bacterium and

28
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:08,420
how much you spread, the agar and its

29
00:01:08,580 --> 00:01:11,700
depth, the disc size, and the incubation time

30
00:01:11,740 --> 00:01:12,580
and temperature.

31
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:17,560
You also need a negative control: a blank

32
00:01:17,640 --> 00:01:19,720
disc dipped in sterile water.

33
00:01:19,960 --> 00:01:22,040
It should have no zone, which shows the

34
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:24,200
paper and water don't stop growth on their

35
00:01:24,280 --> 00:01:24,840
own.

36
00:01:25,080 --> 00:01:27,720
And use three plates, each with all four

37
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:31,000
discs in different positions, so one odd plate,

38
00:01:31,080 --> 00:01:33,400
or one patch of agar, can't decide the

39
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:34,040
result.

40
00:01:36,067 --> 00:01:39,426
Your teacher supplies an approved harmless culture.

41
00:01:39,747 --> 00:01:42,386
Spread point one of a millilitre evenly over

42
00:01:42,427 --> 00:01:44,826
the agar with a sterile spreader, so the

43
00:01:44,867 --> 00:01:47,266
bacteria grow as a smooth lawn.

44
00:01:47,587 --> 00:01:50,466
Then place the discs with sterile forceps, at

45
00:01:50,627 --> 00:01:52,866
least two centimetres apart and away from the

46
00:01:52,947 --> 00:01:55,186
edge, so the zones can't overlap.

47
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:59,680
Then follow your school's procedure, as in the

48
00:01:59,760 --> 00:02:03,120
water testing practical: label the base, close the

49
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:06,240
lid securely, and incubate upside down at twenty

50
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:09,600
five to thirty degrees for two days, never

51
00:02:09,640 --> 00:02:10,880
thirty seven.

52
00:02:10,960 --> 00:02:13,120
From here on, the lids stay shut.

53
00:02:15,134 --> 00:02:17,613
To measure, turn the plate over and lay

54
00:02:17,694 --> 00:02:20,173
a ruler across the base, through the centre

55
00:02:20,214 --> 00:02:21,373
of the disc.

56
00:02:21,454 --> 00:02:23,613
Measure the clear zone edge to edge in

57
00:02:23,694 --> 00:02:24,893
millimetres.

58
00:02:25,054 --> 00:02:27,613
Then turn the ruler a quarter turn, measure

59
00:02:27,814 --> 00:02:29,773
again, and average the two.

60
00:02:30,094 --> 00:02:31,133
No zone at all?

61
00:02:31,374 --> 00:02:34,013
Record six millimetres, the width of the disc

62
00:02:34,094 --> 00:02:34,813
itself.

63
00:02:36,834 --> 00:02:38,073
Here are the results.

64
00:02:38,354 --> 00:02:41,793
Antibiotic A gave twenty four, twenty six and

65
00:02:41,914 --> 00:02:45,393
twenty five millimetres, a mean of twenty five.

66
00:02:45,474 --> 00:02:47,553
B averaged fifteen.

67
00:02:47,754 --> 00:02:49,873
C and the blank disc stayed at six

68
00:02:49,954 --> 00:02:51,113
on every plate.

69
00:02:51,394 --> 00:02:53,953
The repeats agree closely, so the results look

70
00:02:53,994 --> 00:02:54,753
reliable.

71
00:02:54,994 --> 00:02:57,313
And the blank made no clear zone beyond

72
00:02:57,354 --> 00:02:59,873
the disc, so the paper and water didn't

73
00:03:00,034 --> 00:03:00,993
cause the zones.

74
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:06,200
So, on this agar, A produced a larger

75
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:07,400
clear zone than B.

76
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:10,360
But zone size doesn't depend only on how

77
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:11,560
active the drug is.

78
00:03:12,040 --> 00:03:14,040
It also depends on how much drug is

79
00:03:14,120 --> 00:03:15,880
in the disc, and how far it can

80
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:19,240
diffuse: a drug that spreads slowly through agar

81
00:03:19,480 --> 00:03:21,320
can make a small zone even when it

82
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:22,040
works well.

83
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:24,680
So a bigger zone doesn't show that A

84
00:03:24,760 --> 00:03:25,800
is the stronger drug.

85
00:03:26,360 --> 00:03:29,240
And C's missing zone might mean this bacterium

86
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:31,560
simply lacks the part C targets.

87
00:03:33,567 --> 00:03:35,966
A plate also isn't a patient.

88
00:03:36,447 --> 00:03:38,606
To treat an infection, a drug has to

89
00:03:38,727 --> 00:03:40,846
reach the infected tissue at a high enough

90
00:03:40,927 --> 00:03:43,806
dose, without harming the patient, and work on

91
00:03:43,887 --> 00:03:47,726
the actual pathogen, not a harmless teaching strain.

92
00:03:47,847 --> 00:03:50,206
That's what clinical trials test.

93
00:03:50,287 --> 00:03:53,406
So keep the conclusion narrow: A produced a

94
00:03:53,527 --> 00:03:56,366
larger clear zone than B, on this agar,

95
00:03:56,527 --> 00:03:57,806
under these conditions.

96
00:03:59,834 --> 00:04:03,673
Validity: one variable changed, a blank control, and

97
00:04:03,754 --> 00:04:06,873
the same lawn, agar and incubation, so it's

98
00:04:06,914 --> 00:04:09,113
a fair comparison of the zones these discs

99
00:04:09,194 --> 00:04:10,553
make on this bacterium.

100
00:04:11,034 --> 00:04:14,473
Reliability: three plates show whether the zones agree.

101
00:04:14,954 --> 00:04:18,313
Accuracy: a ruler gives a measured diameter, but

102
00:04:18,394 --> 00:04:20,633
a fuzzy edge and the viewing angle limit

103
00:04:20,754 --> 00:04:22,793
how confidently you can place the boundary.

104
00:04:23,274 --> 00:04:25,593
More readings can't sharpen that edge.

105
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:29,000
The risk assessment.

106
00:04:29,280 --> 00:04:31,800
Follow your teacher's approved school procedure.

107
00:04:32,080 --> 00:04:34,720
Even with a harmless culture, a plate can

108
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:38,320
pick up a contaminating microbe, and incubation multiplies

109
00:04:38,400 --> 00:04:38,960
it.

110
00:04:39,040 --> 00:04:42,080
So keep cultured plates closed, never open them

111
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:45,120
to measure the zones, and wash your hands.

112
00:04:45,280 --> 00:04:47,840
Handle discs with forceps, because some people are

113
00:04:47,920 --> 00:04:50,720
allergic to antibiotics like penicillin.

114
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:53,760
Your teacher sterilises used plates in an autoclave

115
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:54,880
before disposal.

116
00:04:56,900 --> 00:04:57,820
Your turn.

117
00:04:58,100 --> 00:05:01,380
A student tested antibiotic discs P and Q

118
00:05:01,540 --> 00:05:03,860
on plates of a harmless bacterium.

119
00:05:04,180 --> 00:05:06,820
The mean zone diameters were twenty two millimetres

120
00:05:06,900 --> 00:05:10,180
for P, thirteen for Q, and six for

121
00:05:10,220 --> 00:05:11,620
a sterile water disc.

122
00:05:12,180 --> 00:05:14,180
She concluded that P would be the more

123
00:05:14,260 --> 00:05:16,580
effective treatment for an infection in people.

124
00:05:17,060 --> 00:05:18,540
Assess her conclusion.

125
00:05:18,820 --> 00:05:20,180
Pause here to answer.

126
00:05:31,400 --> 00:05:33,480
The data support only part of it.

127
00:05:33,960 --> 00:05:36,520
P's twenty two millimetre zone was larger than

128
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:39,880
Q's thirteen, and the six millimetre control made

129
00:05:39,960 --> 00:05:41,080
no zone.

130
00:05:41,200 --> 00:05:44,120
So P produced a larger clear zone, under

131
00:05:44,200 --> 00:05:45,000
these conditions.

132
00:05:45,560 --> 00:05:47,800
That doesn't show which drug treats an infection

133
00:05:47,960 --> 00:05:51,160
better: zone size also depends on dose and

134
00:05:51,240 --> 00:05:54,400
diffusion, and treatment needs clinical trials.

135
00:05:54,680 --> 00:05:57,560
Biggest zone means best medicine is the classic

136
00:05:57,720 --> 00:05:58,520
overclaim.

137
00:06:00,534 --> 00:06:01,093
One more.

138
00:06:01,174 --> 00:06:04,453
A student soaked one paper disc in antiseptic

139
00:06:04,614 --> 00:06:07,573
X for one minute, and another in antiseptic

140
00:06:07,734 --> 00:06:09,573
Y for ten minutes.

141
00:06:09,654 --> 00:06:12,213
She put both on a single plate, incubated

142
00:06:12,294 --> 00:06:14,773
it at thirty seven degrees, then removed the

143
00:06:14,854 --> 00:06:16,773
lid to measure the zones.

144
00:06:16,934 --> 00:06:19,973
Identify two problems, and propose an improvement that

145
00:06:20,054 --> 00:06:21,413
fixes each.

146
00:06:21,494 --> 00:06:22,853
Pause here to answer.

147
00:06:34,067 --> 00:06:37,346
One: the soaking times differed, so the discs

148
00:06:37,467 --> 00:06:39,106
may hold different amounts.

149
00:06:39,427 --> 00:06:41,986
Soak every disc for the same time, or

150
00:06:42,227 --> 00:06:43,746
add the same measured volume.

151
00:06:44,387 --> 00:06:47,346
Two: removing the lid exposed her to whatever

152
00:06:47,427 --> 00:06:50,066
grew, so keep it closed and measure through

153
00:06:50,107 --> 00:06:50,706
the base.

154
00:06:51,267 --> 00:06:53,266
Being more careful opening the lid is the

155
00:06:53,347 --> 00:06:56,146
classic mistake: it shouldn't be opened at all.

156
00:06:58,167 --> 00:07:01,766
So: a lawn of an approved harmless culture,

157
00:07:01,847 --> 00:07:05,286
discs spaced apart, a blank control and three

158
00:07:05,367 --> 00:07:08,486
plates, closed and upside down at twenty five

159
00:07:08,567 --> 00:07:09,686
to thirty degrees.

160
00:07:10,327 --> 00:07:12,566
Measure through the base, and claim only what

161
00:07:12,647 --> 00:07:15,446
the plate shows: which disc gave the larger

162
00:07:15,527 --> 00:07:17,606
clear zone, under these conditions.

